OpenBSD PF reference material for 5BSD PF parity
================================================

Source: https://github.com/openbsd/src.git (OpenBSD CVS mirror)
Revision: facc8d7ec5d1f7a22cd5b7f1e8c6ac4990d91244 (2026-10-10), matching the
  OpenBSD 8.0-current amd64 snapshot used as the reference guest; see
  UPSTREAM.json for the snapshot identity, the PF source-alignment check and
  the git tree object ID of every imported subtree.
Imported: 2026-10-11
License: LICENSE (ISC-style OpenBSD notice); per-file notices retained.

Contents (verbatim, upstream relative paths):
  regress/sbin/pfctl, regress/sys/net/pf_{divert,forward,fragment,opts,
  policy,print,state,table,trans}, regress/sys/net/pflog,
  regress/sys/net/pflow                 primary PF parity suites
  regress/sys/netinet/{frag,pmtu,tcpstate}, regress/sys/netinet6/{frag6,rh0}
                                         IP-stack suites using pf as a tool
                                         (secondary, reported separately)
  share/mk/bsd.regress.mk               OpenBSD regress driver; the upstream
                                         Makefiles include it unchanged

Not present upstream at this revision: regress for pfsync, queues,
syncookies, authpf, pflogd, ftp-proxy/tftp-proxy.

Local changes: none.  Never edit files here to make a test pass; expected
outputs change only through a recorded, user-approved compatibility decision,
and such divergence is kept as a separate, clearly named patch in the glue,
not as an edit in this directory.

5BSD glue: tests/sys/netpfil/pf/openbsd (Kyua/ATF wrapper; installs this
corpus beneath its srctree/ through tests/srctree.mk) and
tools/test/pf-parity/openbsd-regress (two-guest topology runner: OpenBSD
helper as SRC/RT/ECO, DUT = OpenBSD reference or 5BSD).

OpenBSD-derived PF code: whole files adopted for parity are imported here
with provenance and wired in from their native build directories.  Code
merged into FreeBSD-derived sys/netpfil/pf or sbin/pfctl files is recorded
below (OpenBSD file, revision, local destination) and in the commit message.

Merged OpenBSD-derived code (pf/parity):
  (none yet)

Update procedure: fetch the new pinned commit, replace the subtrees,
regenerate UPSTREAM.json (git rev-parse <commit>:<path>), rerun the reference
baseline on the matching signed OpenBSD snapshot, and record any expected
output changes in the PF parity gap report.
